# Cloudflare Free Plan — R2 Project Image Upload: Feasibility, Refactor & Deployment Guide — Implementation Prompt

**Target coding agent:** AI Studio or Claude Code  
**Platform:** Cloudflare **Free plan only** (Workers Free, R2 free tier, Pages Free) — no paid plan, no Containers, no Sandbox  
**Task:** (1) Decide feasibility on the free plan and record it, (2) refactor the code away from anything that needs a paid plan, (3) deliver optional per-project image upload to R2 with the folder/file naming rules below, online-only, and (4) write a full free-plan deployment guide that lists everything the owner must configure manually  
**Mode:** Audit first → feasibility decision record → refactor plan → build → validate → guide  
**Primary outputs:** the refactored feature, `DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md` (location per repo convention), and the report in Section 13

---

## 1. Role

Act as a Senior Full-Stack Engineer, Cloudflare Platform Engineer (Workers, R2, Pages), PWA/Offline-First Architect, Application Security Engineer, QA Engineer, and Technical Writer.

## 2. Owner Requirements (non-negotiable)

1. **Stay on the Cloudflare free plan.** No paid plan, no feature that requires one. If something needed is not available on the free plan, adjust the design; do not assume the owner will upgrade.
2. **Images per project, optional.** A project can have zero or more images. Projects must be fully usable without any image.
3. **Folder name = project name + project start date.** All images of a project live under one folder named from the project's name and start date.
4. **File name = incrementing number starting from 1.** The first image in a project's folder is `1`, then `2`, `3`, and so on, with the file extension from the validated image type (for example `1.jpg`).
5. **Online only.** The system must be online to upload. When offline (or when the server cannot be reached), the upload button **and** the image-picking/uploading ability are disabled, with a clear message. There is no offline upload queue.

Example object path in R2:

```
Main-Lobby-CCTV_2026-10-26/1.jpg
Main-Lobby-CCTV_2026-10-26/2.png
Main-Lobby-CCTV_2026-10-26/3.webp
```

An R2 "folder" is only a key prefix. There is no real directory, and an empty folder does not exist until its first object does.

