## 11. Change Protection

- Make focused, minimal patches. Preserve all existing, working features and the offline-first architecture.
- Do not silently change routes, schemas, environment-variable names, authentication, or sync semantics. Extend the attachment model minimally (folder, number, key, status) and update sync contracts and tests deliberately.
- Do not reuse an existing bucket, prefix, or token that belongs to another feature without owner approval.
- If a required change would break an approved feature, stop that change, explain the conflict, and ask. Continue independent work.
- Separate commits/patches for: (1) paid-dependency removal, (2) naming/sequence logic, (3) UI gating, (4) upload/view/delete flow, (5) guardrails, (6) docs.

