## 12. Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Feasibility Decision Record exists and states plainly that Containers/Sandbox are not usable on the free plan.
- [ ] No Containers, Sandbox, Docker, or paid-plan dependency remains in the deploy path.
- [ ] Images are optional per project; projects work with zero images.
- [ ] Folder name is `{ProjectName}_{StartDate}` (sanitized), assigned at first upload, unique per project, and immutable afterward.
- [ ] Image file names are `1`, `2`, `3`… with the validated extension, per project, never reused, stable across retries.
- [ ] Start date uses the stored date-only value with no timezone shift; missing date uses a fixed placeholder.
- [ ] Upload button and picker are disabled when offline or when the server is unreachable, with the specified messages; there is no offline upload queue.
- [ ] Bucket is private; images are viewed only through short-lived authorized access.
- [ ] R2 token is bucket-scoped, Object Read & Write only (Option A), and no secret is exposed to the browser, repo, logs, or guide.
- [ ] Finalization verifies each uploaded object before it is marked uploaded.
- [ ] Free-tier guardrails (size, count, storage soft cap, compression) are implemented and tested.
- [ ] The privacy trade-off of names in object keys is documented.
- [ ] `DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md` has the Manual Configuration Checklist at the top, matches the procedure, and every step is labeled verified or unverified.
- [ ] Existing features and legacy attachments were not broken or silently renamed.
- [ ] No deployment or cloud-resource change was made without owner authorization.

